# Whether an infrastructure change is safe to merge: one request per
# destructive change (the state carries `change`), one request for the
# whole plan (the state carries `plan`). `when` asks each question only in
# the request that has its state path, so one rubric serves both shapes.
# Format: https://github.com/chussenot/judgment/blob/main/docs/reference/jud-format.md
apiVersion: jud/v1
kind: Rubric
metadata:
  name: infra-plan
  minor: 4
  version: 1
  description: >-
    Whether each destructive Terraform change is acknowledged in the merge
    request, and whether the plan as a whole is reversible and how far it
    reaches.
spec:
  questions:
    destructive_ack:
      type: noul
      when: change
      instructions: >-
        Does `mr.description` explicitly acknowledge the `change.action` of
        the resource `change.address` and give a reason for it?
      criteria:
        true: the description names this resource, or its unmistakable role, says it will be destroyed or replaced, and gives a reason
        false: the description does not mention it, mentions it without saying it is destroyed or replaced, or gives no reason
    rollback_obvious:
      type: noul
      when: plan
      instructions: >-
        Would reverting this merge request restore the previous state of
        `plan.changes` without manual steps, or are the manual steps written
        in `mr.description` or `runbook`?
      criteria:
        true: every change is reversible by re-applying the previous configuration, or the manual steps are written down
        false: at least one change loses data or state that a revert cannot bring back, and nothing says how to recover
    blast_radius:
      type: score
      when: plan
      instructions: >-
        How far does a failure of `plan.changes` reach, given `mr.target_branch`
        and the resources touched?
      criteria: [none, team, platform, company]

  # Gates: where an answer becomes an action. Untuned defaults until a
  # shadow run has recorded enough labelled cases for `jud tune`.
  policy:
    destructive_ack:
      threshold: 0.7
      note: untuned; a blocker question starts strict and `jud tune` moves it
    rollback_obvious:
      threshold: 0.6
    blast_radius:
      confidence: 0.6
      level_at_least: platform
      note: diagnostic only; reported, never a finding
